{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014xnCZ9NB7ojJ4MiJBRAKVp","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I now have a complete understanding of the pkg/testutils package. Let me provide you with a comprehensive report.\n\n## Summary of pkg/testutils Package\n\n### 1. **DiffTest Struct Fields**\n\nThe `DiffTest` struct (defined at line 46-55 in difftest.go) has the following fields:\n\n```go\ntype DiffTest struct {\n\tName          string              // Identifies the subtest (used with t.Run)\n\tArgs          []string            // Command-line arguments passed to both binaries\n\tStdin         []byte              // Input data to both binaries (nil = EOF, empty = open then close)\n\tEnv           []string            // Environment variables (KEY=VALUE pairs, merged with inherited env)\n\tWorkDir       string              // Working directory for binary execution (defaults to t.TempDir())\n\tExitCode      int                 // Expected exit code (defaults to 0)\n\tNormalize     []NormalizeFunc      // Slice of normalization functions applied to output before comparison\n\tExpectedFiles map[string][]byte    // Map of relative file paths to expected file contents\n}\n```\n\n### 2. **Exit Code Comparison**\n\n**YES**, RunDiffTests compares exit codes. The comparison happens in the `compareOutputs()` function at lines 176-185:\n\n```go\nexitMatch := goRes.exitCode == refRes.exitCode\nif stdoutMatch && stderrMatch && exitMatch {\n    return\n}\nt.Fatalf(\"%s\", formatDivergence(tc, goRes, refRes))\n```\n\nThe exit code divergence is also reported in the error message (lines 196-197).\n\n### 3. **Output File Content Support**\n\n**YES**, it supports comparing output file content. The `ExpectedFiles` field is a `map[string][]byte` that maps relative file paths to their expected contents. Files are checked via the `checkExpectedFiles()` function (lines 211-227), which:\n- Reads each expected file from the working directory\n- Compares the actual content byte-for-byte with the expected content\n- Fails the test if any file is missing or content doesn't match\n\n### 4. **File-Related Fields**\n\nYes, there are file-related fields and capabilities:\n\n- **`ExpectedFiles`**: A map of relative file paths to expected byte content (used to verify output files created by the binaries)\n- **`WorkDir`**: The working directory where the binary executes. Defaults to `t.TempDir()` if not specified\n- The test runner also supports environment variables through the `Env` field\n\n### Key Implementation Details:\n\n- **Stdin handling**: If `Stdin` is nil, binaries receive EOF immediately. An empty non-nil slice `[]byte{}` also produces no bytes but represents an open stdin that is immediately closed.\n- **Environment handling**: The `Env` field defaults to inheriting the test process environment with `LC_ALL=C` applied as an override. New or matching keys are merged in.\n- **Normalization**: The `Normalize` field contains an ordered list of normalization functions applied to both stdout and stderr before comparison. A built-in `TimestampNormalizer` is available.\n- **Comparison**: The function compares stdout, stderr, and exit codes between the Go binary and reference binary. All three must match for the test to pass.\n\nAll source files are located in:\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5160/pkg/testutils/difftest.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5160/pkg/testutils/difftest_test.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5160/pkg/testutils/build.go`"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"45b367c8-a543-4f51-9d2a-6e6621243c42","uuid":"db6db6d3-7c26-48ce-9ea7-8806bffa7b69","timestamp":"2026-05-14T12:35:43.946Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-uni